 "rule": "per-graph Neyman base counts n_g ~ sigma_g/sqrt(c_g) per campaign and stratum (sigma floor 3% of the stratum median, powers of two, >= min-points), normalized to the pilot cost per replicate; stratum Neyman multiplier m ~ sqrt(V1/C1) split into replicates r in [min-replicates, max-replicates] (powers of two, equal for campaigns a and b of one sector and loop, the largest not above the smallest positive multiplier of the sector and loop: F11) and a power-of-two sample multiplier s >= 1 per stratum; integer allocation adjusted to the target (with the variance margin) or the budget by optimize(): from the F11 and the Stage-5 split, the greedy loop, a prune pass (target) and a bounded local lattice search over the power-of-two allocations held to the per-batch caps, the better start kept (F11 on ties; OPTIMIZER, recorded as optimizer); allocated cost = task seconds / (eta_omp,g x eta_node); minimum batch count from the per-batch caps",
 "optimizer": {
  "rule": "F13 and the F11 follow-up (2026-10-05, Stage 6): for each split rule, the F11 rule (r from the smallest multiplier of the sector and loop) and the Stage-5 rule (r from the largest): split, the greedy loop (target: double the most efficient s until the target holds; budget: halve s, then r, until the budget holds), then (target only) a prune pass that halves one active stratum's allocation r x s while the predicted SE still meets the target (the halving saving the most, repeated to a fixed point; it stops at the first best halving that fails a per-batch cap), then a local lattice search over the active strata's power-of-two allocations a_k = r x s_k: every combination of a_k x 2^d, |d| <= 2, in a box around a centre (first the split point, then the incumbent, recentred after every improvement; at most 32 boxes), solved exactly per box by meet in the middle; target: least cost subject to SE <= target, budget: least SE subject to cost <= budget; ties by (the other quantity, then the box order); a candidate is accepted only if tools/design.py evaluate_design confirms it and it meets every per-batch cap (at most 16 cap failures per box). r of a (sector, L) is min(r after the greedy loop, the smallest allocation of its active strata) (a sector and loop with a zero-variance stratum keeps its r), s_k = a_k / r. The design kept is the better of the two rules (F11 on ties): never costlier (target) or less precise (budget) than either rule's greedy design at the same batch count K; its predicted SE is evaluate_design's, exact for the integer allocation",
